{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osfans/trime/pulls/2186","id":4960532208,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAivEQM8AAAABJ6u28A","html_url":"https://github.com/osfans/trime/pull/2186","diff_url":"https://github.com/osfans/trime/pull/2186.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/osfans/trime/pull/2186.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osfans/trime/issues/2186","number":2186,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"fix(jni): handle standard UTF-8 and UTF-16 positions","user":{"login":"X2M7","id":239118790,"node_id":"U_kgDODkCpxg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/239118790?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7","html_url":"https://github.com/X2M7","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Typing `a` can expose the supplementary Hanzi `𠼞` in the stock Pinyin candidates (the pinned luna-pinyin dictionary maps that exact word to `a`). On an API21 x86_64 emulator with CheckJNI, returning that candidate aborts in `NewStringUTF`: Rime supplies standard UTF-8, while that JNI API expects Modified UTF-8.\n\nConvert native strings explicitly to UTF-16 with `NewString`, and Java UTF-16 strings to owned standard UTF-8. Use the same UTF-16 code units for preedit length, cursor and selection positions. Preserve the original pending exception and validate converted input before Rime/OpenCC side effects; discard incomplete string arrays. Malformed text is replaced with U+FFFD. Native C-string consumers retain their existing embedded-NUL termination behavior.\n\nThis is a standalone correction based on `12ffd16f`: eight production JNI files plus four native test/documentation files. It includes the signedness, return-move and aggregate-initialization fixes needed for the strict native checks. It does not change T9 layouts/schemas, Kotlin/UI behavior, submodule pins or fork release configuration. Existing `JEnv`/`GlobalRef` ownership code is unchanged.\n\nValidation so far:\n\n- The original API21 CheckJNI abort and tombstone are retained.\n- 115 real checked-JVM Unicode assertions and 46 real-JVM composition-position assertions pass. The same two tests against the upstream headers fail on their expected supplementary-character checks.\n- All six upstream JNI translation units compile for NDK28/API21 x86_64 with `-Wall -Wextra -Werror`.\n- [Fresh exact-source cloud checks](https://github.com/X2M7/trime/actions/runs/39701967075) passed all 301 application JVM cases and the 115 + 46 checked-JVM assertions with both expected upstream negative controls. Original XMLs/streams, source and all 20 recursive pins were verified.\n- [Fork Debug/native build](https://github.com/X2M7/trime/actions/runs/39701935883) and [upstream PR build](https://github.com/osfans/trime/actions/runs/39704066636) each passed all four OS jobs; the original four ABI APKs were checked for package/source, ELF ABI and valid signatures. On API21 with CheckJNI already enabled, the original `e16ab85f` APK survives real stock `a` candidates including `𠼞` in the same PID; real `ni` + Space commits `你`. Compact and expanded candidate rows rendered blank in that API21 observation, so visible selection and whole-app acceptance are explicitly not passed.\n\n- On API35, the same original APK records `Late-enabling -Xcheck:jni` in the actual app PID12444, completes first maintenance, and survives stock `a` with the native supplementary phrase `𠼞`. Native logs report 14 candidates and actual `luna_pinyin` / ASCII=false status; that count is not Java-array introspection. Real Delete, `ni` and Space then commit exactly `你` in the editor, with the same PID and start time. Ordinary candidate rows are visible on API35, so the API21 rendering gap is not generalized to both versions. The rare candidate was not visibly selected or committed.\n\n[API35 original frames, source identity and independent qualification](https://github.com/X2M7/trime/tree/contrib/split-index/doc/contribution-split/checks/jni-unicode-api35-20261022) retain the full scope. The observer authenticated its normal stop and its actual host process exited0; the temporary CheckJNI property and original input method were restored. Original launch/packaging precondition failures and runtime warnings are retained.\n\nThe host tests and the two Android smoke checks cover separate scopes. This does not claim whole-application or TalkBack acceptance, arbitrary native allocation-exception handling, other-ABI runtime acceptance, Release/Lint validation, or zero dependency/toolchain warnings.\n\nJNI string contracts: [Modified UTF-8](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/25/docs/specs/jni/types.html#modified-utf-8-strings), [NewString](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/25/docs/specs/jni/functions.html#newstring).\n","created_at":"2026-10-22T01:09:44Z","updated_at":"2026-10-23T03:59:09Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"009a6e643ead0da836102df02370ed5901c938d2","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osfans/trime/pulls/2186/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osfans/trime/pulls/2186/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osfans/trime/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osfans/trime/issues/2186/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osfans/trime/statuses/2ad1865fd97f09ffba231e5c0e23092cd383b059","head":{"label":"X2M7:contrib/pr-jni-unicode-transport","ref":"contrib/pr-jni-unicode-transport","sha":"2ad1865fd97f09ffba231e5c0e23092cd383b059","user":{"login":"X2M7","id":239118790,"node_id":"U_kgDODkCpxg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/239118790?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7","html_url":"https://github.com/X2M7","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":1252010092,"node_id":"R_kgDOSqAobA","name":"trime","full_name":"X2M7/trime","private":false,"owner":{"login":"X2M7","id":239118790,"node_id":"U_kgDODkCpxg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/239118790?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7","html_url":"https://github.com/X2M7","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/X2M7/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api